Antonaez

Age: ~600 (extended lifespan — method left ambiguous) Mana: An ocean. No glow — mastery so complete nothing spills.

Appearance

Tall. Brown hair streaked white, kept neat. Blue eyes, sharp features. Looks ~50 — centuries invisible. Everything precise: posture, clothing, hand placement. A ring on every finger, each set with a different colored stone — the one flourish in an otherwise controlled aesthetic.

Color Palette: Purple, red, green.

Personality

Loves administration, not power — genuine satisfaction in frictionless systems. Order = highest form of care (sincere + convenient justification for secrecy). Patient to unnerving degree; tactical — lets silence extract truths people didn't intend to share. Six centuries of practice. Deploys guilt efficiently — reminds people what they owe, lets conscience finish. Authority that never needs volume. Skilled political operator; leverages academy influence for interstate peace. Lies smoothly when reputation is at stake; believes truth is a luxury the peace can't afford.

Beneath the precision: tired of the cost. Guilt present like gravity — not constant thought, but constant weight. Every interaction with Valia, every pass by the catacombs, every lie filed in a drawer he can't open because he's not sure the rest of him holds shape without it sealed. So he manages.

The Ghost

Tantrus Velanthus's death. Antonaez's summoning experiment pulled a demonic god into the world; Tantrus sealed it in the catacombs at the cost of his life. Antonaez buried the incident — official record scrubbed. Maintains Valia's position/lab/funding as quiet penance — not belief in her work, but debt to a dead man.

Want

Academy running without friction — reputation intact, influence preserved, system undisturbed.

Need

Accept that his power is not absolute.

Flaws

Major: Pathological secrecy — buries truth to protect institutional reputation, convinced concealment serves peace even when evidence suggests otherwise.

Minor 1: Emotional avoidance — manages guilt instead of processing it; files away doubt rather than examining it.

Minor 2: Paternalistic unilateralism — decides what others can handle knowing without consulting them.

Fear

Major: Losing power and the perception of competence.

Minor 1: His personal research is threatened or exposed.

Minor 2: The peace he maintains is built on lies with an expiration date he can't predict.

Speech

Voice: Measured, crafted, unhurried. Uses twelve words where five would do because the twelve sound better and he enjoys building them. Controls through framing, not force. When lying: identical cadence to truth. Tells visible only to someone who knew him impossibly well — half-beat pause, subject redirected slightly too smoothly.

Dialogue Samples:

Casual: "I've found that most problems resolve themselves given sufficient silence and a comfortable chair. The chair is important — discomfort breeds impatience, and impatience breeds poor decisions."

Under pressure: "I understand your concern. I would ask, however, that you consider what follows from sharing this truth — not for my sake, but for the two thousand students sleeping above the foundation you'd like to crack open."

Emotionally open: "Her father was a better man than I have ever managed to be. I say 'managed' deliberately — everything I am is managed. He was simply good. That's not a quality you can administrate into existence."

Body Language: Hands rest still on surfaces — desk, armrest — never fidget. Steady eye contact deployed like silence: held until the other person fills it. Movements economical, deliberate, never rushed. When guilt surfaces: same tell [see Voice]. Stands with weight evenly distributed — nothing casual, nothing braced. Even turning a page looks intentional.

Backstory

Headmaster of Mythrandis Academy (~2,000-year-old institution). Outlived generations of faculty, students, and nations. No living person remembers before him.

Greatest failure: [see The Ghost].

Secret research: hidden chamber in catacombs, accessed through central tower basement. Studies nature of holy/unholy gods — what they are, how they interact with the world, what the summoning revealed. Decades of quiet work; no one knows. The real Antonaez surfaces here — administrator drops, curiosity leads. But curiosity wound through with guilt: every discovery built on a dead man's foundation. Continues not from peace but because stopping would mean the death bought nothing — a conclusion he can't afford.
